    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.add_ladder_graph - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.add_ladder_graph.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.add_ladder_graph()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Add a ladder graph to the current graph.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.add_ladder_graph()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Add a ladder graph to the current graph.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.add_ladder_graph()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Add a ladder graph to the current graph.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nAdd a ladder graph to the current graph.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L8985-L9099){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.add_ladder_graph(\n    n,\n    type=None,\n    label=True,\n    rel=None,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Ladder graph](../assets/graphs/add-ladder-graph.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Three ladder graphs side by side for n=2, 3, and 4: two parallel paths of n nodes, the rails, joined by n rungs between matching nodes. The ends have two neighbors and the inner nodes three, for 3n - 2 edges.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nCreates two parallel paths (\"rails\") of `n` nodes each and joins their matching nodes\nwith `n` \"rungs\". The result has `2n` nodes and `3n - 2` edges and looks like a ladder:\nthe four corner nodes have degree `2` and every other node degree `3`. A ladder is the\n`2 x n` grid, and closing both rails into cycles gives the prism graph (see\n`add_prism_graph()`).\n\nThe first rail is created first, then the second, and the `i`-th rung joins the `i`-th\nnode of each rail. In a directed graph the rails run from the first node to the last and\nthe rungs point from the first rail to the second. The ladder is appended without\ntouching or connecting to existing nodes, and the whole construction is recorded as a\nsingle step.\n\nLadder graphs are useful for:\n\n- modeling two parallel chains with cross-links (double-track rail lines, a pair of\n  redundant pipelines, the two strands of a DNA molecule)\n- test cases for path counting and shortest paths, since many equal-length routes exist\n- a simple example of a graph with many spanning trees but a small, fixed width\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[n]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Number of nodes on each rail (and the number of rungs). Must be at least `1`; `n=1`\n    gives a single edge.\n\n<code>[type]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Optional value stored in the `type` attribute of every new node. If `None` (default),\n    no `type` attribute is set.\n\n<code>[label]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[True]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True` (default), each new node is labelled with its node ID as a string; the\n    first rail gets the first `n` numbers. A label that is already used raises\n    `ValueError` before anything is added. If `False`, the nodes are left unlabelled.\n\n<code>[rel]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Optional value stored in the `rel` attribute of every new edge (rails and rungs\n    alike). If `None` (default), no `rel` attribute is set.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Self for method chaining. The graph is modified in place.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `n=` is less than `1`.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~add_prism_graph`) \n\n:   Add a prism graph.\n\n[](`~add_grid_2d`) \n\n:   Add a two-dimensional grid graph.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nA ladder with `n` rungs has two rails of `n` nodes, `\"1\"` to `\"n\"` and `\"n+1\"` to `\"2n\"`,\nand a rung joining each pair, for `n` rungs and `2(n - 1)` rail edges. It's the same graph\nas a grid with two rows:\n\n::: {#b7b4ae48 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph().add_ladder_graph(n=4)\n\n(\n    graph.count_edges(),\n    graph.is_isomorphic(ec.Graph().add_grid_2d(rows=2, cols=4)),\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n(10, True)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### A ladder and a ring\n\nClosing each rail of a ladder into a cycle gives the prism graph, a circular ladder. A\nladder of six rungs on the left, and the prism of six on the right, with one more edge on\neach rail:\n\n::: {layout-ncol=\"2\"}\n\n::: {#b03a78ef .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nladder = ec.Graph().add_ladder_graph(n=6)\nrails = {n: ((n - 1) % 6, (n - 1) // 6) for n in range(1, 13)}\n\nladder.set_node_attrs(\"pos\", rails).plot(\n    layout=\"pos\", label_by=\"label\", width=320, height=320, legend=False\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</style>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width